IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `il38-nouns`
IMPORT `il38-xrefs`

-- Tests for the cross-references of the Courts Law provisions in scope. Row IL-38. A reference agrees when what the citing text says it points at is what the target says it is.
-- Positive control: a pair made to disagree must come out as disagreeing.

§ `Each cross-reference agrees`

#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref s 6 to Basic Law s 4` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref s 6(2) to Basic Law s 4(f)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref s 6(3B) to Basic Law s 4(f)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref s 6B(a) to Basic Law s 4(b)(1)(b) to (d)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref s 6B(c)(2) to Knesset Law s 61` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref s 6C(a) to Courts Law s 2` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref s 6C(b) to Knesset Law s 6` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref s 8(a) to Basic Law s 4(a)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref s 8(a) to Basic Law s 4(d)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref s 14(a) to Basic Law s 7(4)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref s 25(b) to Courts Law s 2(1)` EQUALS TRUE

§ `The whole list, and the control`

#ASSERT count `the cross-references of the Courts Law provisions in scope` EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `every cross-reference in the list agrees` `the cross-references of the Courts Law provisions in scope` EQUALS TRUE

`a pair made to disagree` MEANS
    `A cross-reference` OF "control", "control", `a Knesset member's secession from a faction`, `the election of its members to a committee`

#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `a pair made to disagree` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `every cross-reference in the list agrees` (LIST `a pair made to disagree`) EQUALS FALSE
